    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n74660" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὀπτ-ήρια</span></b>  (sc. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δῶρα</span>), τά, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>presents made by the bridegroom on seeing the
				bride without the veil,</i>
			
				=
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀνακαλυπτήρια, θεώρητρα</span>
			, <i><span class="en">
				Poll.
				2.59
			</span></i>,<i><span class="en">
				3.36
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Hsch.
			</span></i>
		</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b> generally, <i>presents
				upon seeing</i> or <i>for the sight of</i> a person, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">παιδὸς ὀ.</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					E.
					<u>Ion</u>
					1127
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Call.
				<u>Dian.</u>
				74
			</span></i> ; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">προσβάλλων ἀκοαῖς ὀ.
			θυμοῦ</span> Aspasia ap.<i><span class="en">
				Ath.
				5.219d
			</span></i>.</div>
